; 3DLmon.inf
;
; 3D labs information file for monitors.
; The data contained here is read by the 3Dlabs
; display control panel extension to configure 
; and set-up user monitors.
;
; The file syntax is:
;
; Mode     = X,Y,refresh
; Range    = x,  y,  X,   Y,   fh,  FH,  fv,FV, pclk, PClk
; Example  = 640,480,1920,1200,30.0,96.0,50,160,23.00,253.00
; Detailed = raw EDID detailed timing data
; Timing   = HFP,  HSW,     HBP,  HA,          VFP,  VSW,     VBP,  VA,          Pclk,      HSP,         VSP,         Xmm, Ymm
;            HorFP,HorSyncW,HorBP,HorActive(?),VerFP,VerSyncW,VerBP,VerActive(?),Pixelclock,HorSyncPorch,VerSyncPorch, ??, ??
; Example  = 32,   160,     304,  1600,        3,    3,       40,   1024,        170.450,   -,           -,           474, 296
; Flags    = None, one or more of the following:
;				AddExtras			Add in extra modes which the ranges given
;				LimitXY				When adding extra modes, limit according to resolution as well as frequency
;				DigiSig				The monitor uses digital signalling (DVI-D, DFP)
;				DigiConForceOn			The monitor uses a digital connector (DVI-I, DVI-D, DVI-A, DFP)
;				DigiConForceOff			The monitor uses an analogue connector (VGA)
;
; Date: 11/9/2000
; Version 2.2
; Copyright (c) 2000, 3Dlabs Incorporated
;
; Date 11.07.2003
; Modified by Cyviz AS (www.cyviz.com)
; Added timing information for xpo.1, xpo.2 and vizwall configurations
; Added EDID data for xpo

